+# Agents-management lockstep release and rollback plan
+
+Task: `TASK-260830-s5ro4e`
+
+Date: 2026-08-30
+
+## Decision
+
+Do not land a breaking agents-management contract before both consumers have
+shipped against the generalized graph. Use `skill-agents-management v0.5.0` as
+the compatibility bridge, migrate and release task-board first, then migrate
+and release agents-infra. Only then may a separately reviewed
+`skill-agents-management v0.6.0` remove the legacy compatibility adapters.
+
+This order creates no interval in which the running board dynamically loads an
+unsupported contract. Go resolves and compiles the pinned module into each
+binary. Publishing a newer module tag does not change a running or installed
+task-board binary.
+
+Reserved release versions for this sequence:
+
+- `skill-agents-management v0.5.0` at
+  `b74f758a90a422304d55460422831da80e3d6cc8` — already released; compatibility
+  bridge and inference-engine contract.
+- `skill-project-management 0.25.0` — first task-board release migrated to the
+  generalized graph, pinned to `skill-agents-management v0.5.0`.
+- `relux-agents-infra v1.7.0` — first agents-infra release consuming the same
+  graph, pinned to `skill-agents-management v0.5.0`.
+- `skill-agents-management v0.6.0` — first version allowed to remove legacy
+  compatibility adapters; conditional on the pre-release gates below.
+- `skill-project-management 0.25.1` and `relux-agents-infra v1.7.1` — patch
+  releases that repin the already-migrated consumers to `v0.6.0`.
+
+The reserved versions are part of this plan. If any is already occupied before
+execution, stop and revise this reviewed plan; do not silently substitute a
+different version.
+
+## Measured task-board consumption surface
+
+Baseline inspected:
+
+- task-board source: `skill-project-management` commit
+  `063197b1` (`0.24.3-172-g063197b1` when built with repository metadata).
+- installed task-board: `0.24.3-172-g063197b1`.
+- required module: `skill-agents-management v0.2.0` at
+  `tools/board-cli/go.mod:10`, with a vendored copy.
+
+The source census excludes `vendor/**`, generated module files, and tests unless
+the row says otherwise.
+
+| Measurement | Result |
+| --- | ---: |
+| Production Go files importing agents-management | 26 |
+| Test Go files importing agents-management | 38 |
+| Direct public package families | 13 |
+| Compiled agents-management packages, including transitive internals | 17 |
+| Production LOC in the 26 direct consumer files | 11,862 |
+| Direct raw `pkg/plugin` imports | 0 |
+| Direct `pkg/inferenceengine` imports | 0 |
+
+The 13 direct package families are `pkg/agentic`, six system plugins (`agy`,
+`claude`, `codex`, `gemini`, `muse`, `qwen`), `pkg/providerlimits`,
+`pkg/vendorplugin`, and four vendor registrations (`alibaba`, `anthropic`,
+`google`, `openai`).
+
+The coupling is dense but narrower than the task title suggests:
+
+1. Launch construction uses `agentic.Registry`, six system constructors,
+   `LaunchRequest`, `BuildPlan`, all three launch modes, capability/effort
+   declarations, composition, goals, budget, service tier, run context and the
+   resulting `Plan`. The production dispatch is
+   `internal/spawn/launch_plan.go:332-342`; process execution remains in
+   task-board.
+2. Model selection uses `vendorplugin.Default`, runtime declarations, vendor
+   and system IDs, lineup/lifecycle, model metadata, pricing and four init-time
+   vendor registrations. A custom `qwen-codex` runtime is declared through the
+   compatibility registry.
+3. The largest surface is `pkg/providerlimits`: provider classification,
+   identity resolution, state stores, leases, liveness, group tables, ladders,
+   spread cursors, observations, reports and reset hints. This is operationally
+   critical to spawn admission but is not the generalized plugin graph.
+4. task-board does not call the raw generalized registry or the inference-engine
+   contract today. `v0.5.0` publishes existing `agentic.Registry` and
+   `vendorplugin.Registry` as compatibility bridges backed by `pkg/plugin`.
+
+Therefore the immediate risk is compatibility-adapter regression across a
+large caller surface, not a direct dependency on every new graph type.
+
+## Compatibility matrix
+
+| task-board | agents-management compiled into it | agents-infra | Support status |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `0.24.3-172-g063197b1` | `v0.2.0` | `v1.6.1-100-gd69a435` | Current known-working baseline. agents-infra does not import the module. |
+| Source `063197b1` scratch build | `v0.5.0` | unchanged | Source-compatible bridge proven by the bounded evidence below; not a shipped combination. |
+| `0.25.0` | `v0.5.0` | `v1.6.1-100-gd69a435` | Supported transition after task-board release. |
+| `0.25.0` | `v0.5.0` | `v1.7.0` | Target non-breaking migrated combination. |
+| Installed `0.25.0` | still embeds `v0.5.0` | installed `v1.7.0` | Remains supported while `v0.6.0` is merely published. No dynamic repin occurs. |
+| `0.25.1` | `v0.6.0` | `v1.7.1`, also pinned to `v0.6.0` | Target post-compatibility-cleanup combination. |
+
+No consumer may use an untagged agents-management commit, a `replace`, or a
+workspace override in a release build.
+
+## Required board capability gate
+
+At every step the currently installed board must retain all of these, not only
+parse a config:
+
+- `spawn`: task-specific preflight, run-record creation, provider launch,
+  status/observe/directives and terminal evidence;
+- route: producer `handoff`, reviewer launch, reviewer verdict and
+  `accept_cr`/rework routing;
+- resource add/update/get, because handoff requires outcome evidence;
+- Story workspace and Change Request reads needed to finish the migration.
+
+Static build/tests are necessary but insufficient. Each consumer release must
+run one real canary spawn and one real producer-to-reviewer route on the live
+board before it becomes the default binary. The canary must attach a
+task-scoped outcome, hand off, and receive an explicit reviewer verdict. A
+failed canary is routed with the saved old binary and triggers rollback; it is
+never relabelled green.
+
+## Release order and rollback
+
+### Step 0 — freeze the working recovery point
+
+Repositories and versions:
+
+- task-board: `skill-project-management` commit `063197b1`, installed version
+  `0.24.3-172-g063197b1`, compiled with agents-management `v0.2.0`;
+- agents-infra: installed `v1.6.1-100-gd69a435` at
+  `d69a435945758ea1cd5dfa62395ca32498e712c7`;
+- agents-management: `v0.5.0` at
+  `b74f758a90a422304d55460422831da80e3d6cc8`.
+
+Before any migration task starts, save executable copies and hashes under a
+task-scoped operator directory. Do not stop or restart any run:
+
+```bash
+TB_RECOVERY_ROOT="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/task-board-lockstep.XXXXXX")"
+mkdir -p "$TB_RECOVERY_ROOT/bin"
+cp "$(command -v task-board)" "$TB_RECOVERY_ROOT/bin/task-board"
+cp "$(command -v tb-sessiond)" "$TB_RECOVERY_ROOT/bin/tb-sessiond"
+cp "$(command -v agents-infra)" "$TB_RECOVERY_ROOT/bin/agents-infra"
+shasum -a 256 "$TB_RECOVERY_ROOT"/bin/*
+"$TB_RECOVERY_ROOT/bin/task-board" --version
+"$TB_RECOVERY_ROOT/bin/agents-infra" version
+```
+
+Required-working capabilities: run a read-only spawn preflight with the saved
+task-board, then use the installed board for one ordinary spawn/status/resource
+round trip. Existing in-flight runs continue on their already-exec'd process
+images.
+
+Rollback: this step changes no product state. Deleting the recovery directory
+is not a rollback and must wait until the whole sequence is accepted.
+
+Rollback status: **UNTESTED operationally**. This task inspected versions but
+did not copy or restore installed binaries.
+
+### Step 1 — hold agents-management at the compatibility bridge
+
+Repository/version: `skill-agents-management v0.5.0` at exact commit
+`b74f758a90a422304d55460422831da80e3d6cc8`. It is already published; this
+plan performs no tag or release action.
+
+Required-working capabilities: current task-board remains installed and still
+embeds `v0.2.0`; `spawn`, route and resource operations are unchanged. Before
+changing task-board source, a clean scratch copy of its exact candidate base
+must build and pass spawn tests against public `v0.5.0` with `GOWORK=off` and
+no module replace.
+
+In-flight runs: unaffected. Publishing a Go module tag does not replace code in
+an already-running task-board or child process.
+
+Source rollback command if the dependency-only candidate fails:
+
+```bash
+cd /path/to/skill-project-management/tools/board-cli
+GOWORK=off go mod edit \
+  -require=github.com/relux-works/skill-agents-management@v0.2.0
+GOWORK=off go mod tidy
+GOWORK=off go mod vendor
+GOWORK=off go test -mod=vendor ./internal/spawn -count=1
+GOWORK=off go build -mod=vendor ./...
+```
+
+Rollback status: **PARTIALLY TESTED**. In a scratch archive of `063197b1`,
+repinning `v0.5.0 -> v0.2.0`, building the CLI, reading the authoritative task
+and running spawn-preflight all exited 0. The full suite and workstation install
+restore were not exercised.
+
+### Step 2 — migrate and release task-board first
+
+Repository/version: `skill-project-management 0.25.0`, pinned exactly to
+`skill-agents-management v0.5.0` and migrated by `TASK-260830-mf1xwk`.
+
+Why first: task-board is the control plane that must remain capable of spawning
+and routing the agents-infra migration. agents-infra remains at
+`v1.6.1-100-gd69a435` during this step.
+
+Required-working capabilities and evidence, in order:
+
+1. Keep the saved `0.24.3-172-g063197b1` binary as the command used to route
+   the migration task until the candidate canary passes.
+2. On the exact reviewed `0.25.0` head, run the complete task-board suite,
+   build all binaries, and verify the module graph contains public `v0.5.0`
+   with no replace.
+3. Run the candidate CLI's read/query, `project_config(view=spawn-preflight)`,
+   one real canary spawn, resource handoff, reviewer spawn and reviewer verdict
+   on the live board.
+4. Only after that canary succeeds, install/tag/release `0.25.0` and make it the
+   default `task-board` binary. Re-run the same live spawn-and-route canary from
+   the installed binary.
+
+In-flight runs: do not cancel them. A running `task-board spawn` process keeps
+the old executable image after on-disk replacement, and its provider child is
+already launched. Its later board mutations remain valid because this step
+does not change board storage schemas. Existing `tb-sessiond` processes also
+keep their old image; do not restart them during active sessions. New commands
+use `0.25.0` only after the canary gate.
+
+Fast operational rollback, using the Step-0 saved binary:
+
+```bash
+install -m 0755 "$TB_RECOVERY_ROOT/bin/task-board" \
+  "$HOME/.local/bin/.task-board.rollback"
+mv -f "$HOME/.local/bin/.task-board.rollback" "$HOME/.local/bin/task-board"
+"$HOME/.local/bin/task-board" --version
+"$HOME/.local/bin/task-board" q --format compact \
+  'project_config(view=spawn-preflight, role=developer, agent=codex, task_class=code)'
+```
+
+Coherent binary/skill/role restore from the exact working source follows after
+the board is reachable:
+
+```bash
+TB_OLD_SOURCE="$TB_RECOVERY_ROOT/skill-project-management-063197b1"
+git -C /path/to/skill-project-management worktree add --detach \
+  "$TB_OLD_SOURCE" 063197b1
+"$TB_OLD_SOURCE/scripts/setup.sh" --install-only
+task-board --version
+```
+
+Rollback status: **UNTESTED operationally**. No installed binary, skill or role
+was replaced by this planning task. The source-level v0.2.0 rebuild/query
+rehearsal is not evidence that workstation restore works.
+
+### Step 3 — migrate and release agents-infra
+
+Repository/version: `relux-agents-infra v1.7.0`, pinned exactly to
+`skill-agents-management v0.5.0`, after `TASK-260830-y6infr` and
+`TASK-260830-11ajl2`. task-board stays at `0.25.0`.
+
+Required-working capabilities:
+
+- task-board `0.25.0` must still complete spawn-preflight and route while
+  agents-infra is built and tested;
+- agents-infra's existing compose, prepare, primary-session, target, Pi,
+  runtime and model-check gates must remain green;
+- a real task-board canary must exercise the production agents-infra compose
+  seam, launch a child, attach its outcome and route it through review;
+- Pi/runtime process ownership remains agents-infra; no broker or in-flight
+  local runtime is restarted merely to change the consumer library.
+
+In-flight runs: existing provider children and task-board monitors do not load
+the new agents-infra binary. Existing primary sessions and Pi runtimes continue
+under the old process image. Do not kill them. New compositions use `v1.7.0`
+only after its canary passes.
+
+Rollback to the saved installed binary:
+
+```bash
+install -m 0755 "$TB_RECOVERY_ROOT/bin/agents-infra" \
+  "$HOME/.local/bin/.agents-infra.rollback"
+mv -f "$HOME/.local/bin/.agents-infra.rollback" "$HOME/.local/bin/agents-infra"
+"$HOME/.local/bin/agents-infra" version
+"$HOME/.local/bin/agents-infra" verify global
+task-board q --format compact \
+  'project_config(view=spawn-preflight, role=developer, agent=codex, task_class=code)'
+```
+
+Coherent source restore, if the installed runtime surface also changed:
+
+```bash
+AI_OLD_SOURCE="$TB_RECOVERY_ROOT/relux-agents-infra-d69a435"
+git -C /path/to/relux-agents-infra worktree add --detach \
+  "$AI_OLD_SOURCE" d69a435945758ea1cd5dfa62395ca32498e712c7
+"$AI_OLD_SOURCE/setup.sh"
+agents-infra verify global
+```
+
+Rollback status: **UNTESTED**. This planning task did not replace the installed
+agents-infra executable or runtime surface.
+
+### Step 4 — only then allow the breaking contract release
+
+Repository/version: conditional `skill-agents-management v0.6.0`.
+
+Precondition: `0.25.0` and `v1.7.0` are both released, installed-canary green,
+and no production source imports the compatibility APIs proposed for removal.
+Create clean scratch copies of both exact release tags, repin them to the exact
+`v0.6.0` candidate commit, and run their full tests/builds plus the task-board
+live read/preflight canary before tagging agents-management.
+
+Required-working capabilities: the installed task-board remains `0.25.0` and
+continues embedding `v0.5.0`; its spawn and route behavior does not change when
+the `v0.6.0` tag is published.
+
+In-flight runs: unaffected. No installed process dynamically resolves the new
+module tag.
+
+Rollback if the candidate fails: do not publish `v0.6.0`; restore scratch
+consumer pins to `v0.5.0`. If a bad immutable tag has already been published,
+do not delete or move it. Keep all consumers pinned to `v0.5.0` and publish a
+new reviewed `v0.6.1` restoring the required surface before any consumer repin.
+
+```bash
+cd /path/to/consumer/tools/board-cli  # or the agents-infra Go module
+GOWORK=off go mod edit \
+  -require=github.com/relux-works/skill-agents-management@v0.5.0
+GOWORK=off go mod tidy
+```
+
+Rollback status: **UNTESTED**. `v0.6.0` does not exist and no adapter removal
+was performed.
+
+### Step 5 — repin migrated consumers to the breaking version
+
+Repositories/versions, in order:
+
+1. `skill-project-management 0.25.1`, pinned to released
+   `skill-agents-management v0.6.0`;
+2. `relux-agents-infra v1.7.1`, pinned to released
+   `skill-agents-management v0.6.0`.
+
+Required-working capabilities: repeat the full candidate and installed
+spawn-and-route canary for `0.25.1` before agents-infra moves; then repeat it
+after `v1.7.1`. The old `0.25.0` and `v1.7.0` binaries remain the recovery
+pair until both canaries and review accept the exact heads.
+
+In-flight runs: same as Steps 2 and 3. Old process images continue; no run is
+killed, restarted or reparented because of the repin.
+
+Rollback: atomically restore task-board `0.25.0` and agents-infra `v1.7.0`
+from the release-specific backups captured immediately before this step, then
+republish forward patch releases (`0.25.2` / `v1.7.2`) pinned to `v0.5.0` if a
+source fix is required. Never rewrite `0.25.1`, `v1.7.1` or `v0.6.0` tags.
+
+Rollback status: **UNTESTED**. None of these releases exists yet.
+
+## Unsupported-contract windows
+
+There are no planned runtime windows in which task-board runs against an
+unsupported agents-management version:
+
+| Potential window | Duration | Impact | Avoidance |
+| --- | ---: | --- | --- |
+| `v0.5.0` exists while current board pins `v0.2.0` | `0s` runtime mismatch | None; the board embeds `v0.2.0`. | Go module pinning; no dynamic loading. |
+| task-board source is being migrated | `0s` installed mismatch | None; saved/current board remains the routing authority. | Candidate is built and canaried out of place. |
+| `0.25.0` is installed while agents-infra remains old | `0s` contract mismatch | Spawn/route remain available; old agents-infra is an independent consumer. | task-board migrates first and the compose seam remains backward compatible. |
+| `v0.6.0` is published before consumer repin releases | `0s` runtime mismatch | None; installed consumers still embed `v0.5.0`. | Do not use `@latest`; exact pins only. |
+| binary replacement on disk | Expected sub-second file operation, but not a contract mismatch | Existing processes continue; a non-atomic installer could briefly make a new invocation fail. | Canary out of place, retain absolute old binary, and use same-filesystem temp-plus-`mv` for the critical CLI rollback/cutover. |
+
+The one prohibited window is editing the only runnable task-board source to a
+breaking dependency and invoking setup before candidate tests pass. Its
+duration would be from the failed install until source/binary restore, with new
+spawn and route commands potentially unavailable. The sequence above avoids
+that window entirely; it is not an accepted degraded mode.
+
+## Validation evidence gathered by this planning task
+
+No migration, release or tag was performed. All dependency changes were made
+only in `.temp/TASK-260830-s5ro4e/` against an archive of exact task-board
+commit `063197b1`.
+
+| Command / gate | Exit | Interpretation |
+| --- | ---: | --- |
+| `go list -mod=mod -m ...skill-agents-management` after scratch pin to `v0.5.0` | 0 | Public module resolved exactly as `v0.5.0`. |
+| `go test -mod=mod ./internal/spawn -count=1` | 1 | Honest red: only `TestCodexArgvGuardCatchesTheHistoricalThreeSites` failed because a `git archive` has no `.git` for its `git show HEAD:...` assertion. Not counted green. |
+| Same spawn package with only that archive-inapplicable guard skipped | 0 | All runnable spawn behavior tests passed against `v0.5.0`. |
+| `go build -mod=mod` candidate CLI against `v0.5.0` | 0 | Consumer compiles. |
+| First candidate CLI invocation | 127 | Operator path typo; no board mutation. Corrected path rerun below. |
+| Candidate CLI `get(...)` and real `project_config(view=spawn-preflight, ...)` | 0 | Authoritative board read and production preflight work against the `v0.5.0` build. |
+| Scratch repin to `v0.2.0` and rebuild | 0 | Source rollback builds. |
+| Rebuilt `v0.2.0` CLI read and spawn-preflight | 0 | Source rollback can read and preflight the authoritative board. |
+
+This evidence proves source compatibility and the bounded source-pin rollback.
+It does not claim a full-suite pass, a real child launch under the candidate,
+or an installed-binary rollback. Those remain mandatory gates for the
+execution tasks.
+
+## Release stop conditions
+
+Stop and roll back instead of forcing the migration if any of these occurs:
+
+- the candidate needs a `replace`, mutable tag, runtime lookup of `latest`, or
+  a second shadow graph to keep task-board working;
+- the old binary cannot route the candidate canary after a candidate failure;
+- a canary can spawn but cannot attach evidence and reach a real reviewer
+  verdict;
+- an in-flight run must be killed or have its record rewritten to survive a
+  step;
+- the proposed compatibility removal still has a production consumer import;
+- a rollback command has not been rehearsed for the environment where it will
+  be used. It remains explicitly **UNTESTED**, not assumed reversible.
